id: pm-gh1642
title: "GH-1642: brief pm list and pm search pages print an envelope as large as their rows; the default sort and search's default omission receipt are no longer compacted"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1642\n\nReproduced on the current source build (2026.10.31). pm list: projectPmBriefListEnvelope (src/sdk/output/list-envelope.ts, pm-6pycus) only drops the default sorting block when it has exactly the keys sort and order. Sorting later gained effective_keys, so the 7-line default sort is printed on every brief list page — the compaction silently stopped matching its own default. filters echoes limit, which applied_limit already states. pm search has no brief projection at all: it prints truncated (equal to has_more), filters {limit} (equal to applied_limit) and a 4-line omission_receipt whose only group is projection_metadata restorable with --full.\n\nDeliberate exclusions, with reasons: completeness unchecked stays visible (pm-6pycus AC: unchecked and partial source evidence cannot become complete or disappear); the items_encoding block stays because it is the lossless decode contract for the matched_fields list column, and the formatter round-trip tests require json_columns and absent to restore rows; JSON, --full and SDK result types keep the full receipts.\n\nDuplicate search: 'brief envelope list', GH-1501, GH-1642; nearest is pm-6pycus (GH-1501 brief list envelope, closed) which this extends."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,github,output,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T01:17:44.606Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:34.335Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:34.335Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "A default brief pm list page drops the legacy default sort/order echo but keeps the effective default comparator order visible on one effective_keys line (the GH-1507 disclosure), and omits a filters.limit equal to applied_limit and empty runtime_filters; a default pm search page, including a terminal page without continuation fields, omits truncated when equal to has_more and a filters block that only echoes applied_limit, and replaces the single default projection_metadata omission receipt with details --full; unchecked or partial completeness, non-default sorting, non-limit filters, custom omission receipts, JSON, --full and SDK results are unchanged; the search projection is a reusable SDK export that leaves its input unchanged; measured envelope bytes drop on a small page"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "projectPmBriefListEnvelope now recognizes the default ascending sort even with effective_keys. It replaces the legacy sort/order echo with one effective_keys comparator line, keeping the GH-1507 disclosure, and drops a filters.limit equal to applied_limit and empty runtime_filters. The new public SDK projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope drops truncated when it repeats has_more and limit-only filters, and replaces the default projection_metadata omission receipt with details --full. formatBuiltInOutput chains both for TOON only. completeness unchecked and items_encoding stay by contract."
expected_result: "Small default pm list and pm search pages print only envelope fields that carry information, while JSON, --full and SDK results keep complete receipts."
actual_result: "Same tracker, published 2026.10.31 vs this branch: pm search 'release workflow' --limit 3 drops from 1,033 to 863 bytes and pm list --status open --limit 3 from 988 to 782 bytes. compact-agent-output spec 59/59 and default-list-order integration pass; the GH-1642 cases fail with the projection stashed. SDK surface update is additive for the new export."
