comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-31T21:47:00.908Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation and measurement: projectPmBriefListEnvelope now drops the default ascending sort when it carries effective_keys (the regression), and drops a filters.limit equal to applied_limit and empty runtime_filters. New public projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope (sdk/output) drops truncated when it equals has_more and limit-only filters, and replaces the single default projection_metadata omission receipt with details --full. It is chained after the list projection in formatBuiltInOutput (TOON only). Measured with the published 2026.10.31 package against this branch on this tracker: pm search 'release workflow' --limit 3 drops from 1,033 to 863 B (-16%) and pm list --status open --limit 3 from 988 to 782 B (-21%). completeness unchecked and items_encoding remain by design (see description)."
  "2026-10-31T21:49:41.855Z","harness:claude-code","Design correction while testing: the 7-line default sort block is not only redundant metadata. GH-1507's accepted contract (pm-zd46m7, integration spec default-list-order) requires brief TOON to disclose the effective default comparator order so an agent knows why rows arrive in that order. Dropping it would undo that decision. The projection therefore drops only the legacy sort/order echo and renders the effective keys on one line, for example sorting.effective_keys 'status_registry:nonterminal_before_terminal asc, priority asc, updated_at desc, id asc'. Seven lines become two, and JSON keeps the full pair array. A malformed or extended sorting block passes through unchanged."
  "2026-10-31T23:02:11.868Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 1 on PR #1645: the list projection left the raw filters key in place when the compacted filters became empty, so a limit-only or empty-runtime filters block still printed. filters is now destructured out of the envelope before compaction, and specs cover {limit}, {runtime_filters:{}} and a non-echo limit."
  "2026-11-01T01:17:44.606Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 2 on PR #1645: a final search page omits has_more, truncated, next_cursor and total, so the projection skipped it. projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope now also accepts that terminal shape when count matches the rows, there is no cursor, and any total equals count; inconsistent shapes still pass through. The acceptance criterion now states that the effective default sort order stays visible on one line, matching the resolution."
